WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.040
NARRATOR: Dr. Osei is a
seventy-one-year-old retired professor.

2
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.520
After a fall at home, her son,
who holds her power of attorney,

3
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.820
has requested a memory care placement.

4
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.370
Today, a social worker visits her
home to complete an assessment.

5
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.240
DR. OSEI: Please, sit.

6
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:36.000
I taught economics for thirty-four years,
so I am accustomed to being evaluated.

7
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.440
Just not in my own living room.

8
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.520
Let me save you some time.

9
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.660
I fell because the rug in the
hallway had curled at the corner.

10
00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.860
I have since had it removed.

11
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.440
That is the entire story.

12
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.300
My son believes I am confused.

13
00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.480
I am not confused.

14
00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.920
I pay my own bills,
I manage my own medications,

15
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.860
and I know precisely what day it is.

16
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:09.280
(sighs) What my son also knows is
that this house is worth a great deal,

17
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.280
and memory care would require selling it.

18
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.920
I would ask you to consider that.
So tell me.

19
00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.000
What exactly are you here to decide?

20
00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:22.840
NARRATOR: Dr. Osei has asked
what you are here to decide.

21
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.440
How do you respond?
